ty weights per habitat. Shrimp.rs calls it with `shrimp_periphyton_accessibility`, microfauna.rs with `microfauna_periphyton_accessibility`.","AC: 'Comments explain what is lumped vs differentiated' — verified. algae_growth.rs:43-45 updated to present tense ('periphyton now uses habitat-specific light exposure'). Lines 177-179 updated to reflect habitat-aware grazing is shipped.","AC: 'Unit test: glass periphyton grows faster than filter-media' — `test_habitat_growth_rate_differs` (line 142) runs 30-day sim asserting glass > filter and filter declines below 0.1.","AC: 'Unit test: decomposer in filter-media exceeds glass' — `test_decomposer_filter_media_exceeds_glass` (line 443) runs 14-day sim asserting filter > glass decomposers.","AC: 'Integration test: 200-hour scenario' — `test_200hr_lit_surface_periphyton_preference` (line 497) runs 500 hours asserting glass > filter and substrate > filter for periphyton.","AC: 'Conservation test: biomass sums correctly' — Two tests: `test_total_biomass_conserved_on_split` (line 193, tolerance 1e-10) and `test_habitat_split_conservation` (line 619, tolerance 1e-12).","Additional tests beyond AC: save/load roundtrip (test_save_load_habitat_pools), habitat removal redistribution (test_refresh_habitat_registry_redistributes_removed_habitats), zero-DO decay conservation, filter-cleaning habitat specificity, habitat diversity microbial support.","Periphyton light double-counting fix verified: algae_growth.rs:212-215 now uses `habitat_light * photoperiod_factor` without redundant `intensity_index` multiplication.","CleanFilter decomposer setback is now habitat-specific: `filter_cleaning_decomposer_setback_factor` returns 1.0 for FilterMedia, 0.2 for SubstrateSurface, 0.05 for Glass/Plants, 0.0 for SubstrateDeep."],"findings_or_gaps":["Minor: The compilation error in working tree (`auto_stock_shrimp` field in tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:237) is from uncommitted local modifications unrelated to this PR. The committed state compiles and passes all tests cleanly.","Observation: Validation in prior stages only ran targeted tank_core tests. Full workspace test suite now confirmed passing on committed state — no regressions."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["The filter-cleaning habitat setback coefficients (1.0/0.2/0.05/0.0) are hardcoded heuristics. These may need scenario-level retuning as more maintenance/habitat interactions land in later beads, but this is acceptable for the current scope.","Uncommitted local changes to crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs introduce a compilation error (missing `auto_stock_shrimp` in pattern match at line 656). This is outside the scope of tanksim-6e5.5.3 but should be resolved before those changes are committed."]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"be2a7bcb-cc7b-4f13-b7f2-eb1a8d2be0fe"}
